1
00:00:00,531 --> 00:00:03,913
(Q1) Good Morning, Youth Council. Caroline speaking.

2
00:00:03,913 --> 00:00:10,296
Oh, hello, I'm interested in standing for election to the Youth Council, and I was told to give you a call.

3
00:00:10,296 --> 00:00:15,636
That's good. Could I have your name, please? Yes, it's Roger Brown.

4
00:00:15,636 --> 00:00:24,021
Thank you. I'm Caroline, the Youth Council administrator. So do you know much about what the Council does, Roger?

5
00:00:24,021 --> 00:00:28,469
I've talked to Stephanie - I think she's the chair of the Council.

6
00:00:28,469 --> 00:00:31,444
That's right. And she told me a lot about it.

7
00:00:31,444 --> 00:00:38,266
How it's a way for young people to discuss local issues, for example, and make suggestions to the town council.

8
00:00:38,266 --> 00:00:40,073
That's what made me interested.&nbsp;

9
00:00:40,073 --> 00:00:44,499
Fine. Well let me take down some of your details.

10
00:00:44,499 --> 00:00:51,503
First of all, how old are you? You know the Council is for young people aged from 13 to 18?

11
00:00:51,503 --> 00:00:53,112
[🟢前一题内容定位] I've just turned 18.&nbsp;

12
00:00:53,112 --> 00:00:58,267
[🟢 live=stay] And where do you live, Roger? Well, that's a bit complicated.

13
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:07,707
[Q1答案句] At the moment I'm looking for a flat to rent here, so I'm in a hostel from Monday to Friday, I go back to my parents' place at the weekend.

14
00:01:07,707 --> 00:01:13,142
(Q2) OK, so where's the best place to send you some information about the Council?

15
00:01:13,142 --> 00:01:15,511
Oh，to my parents' address, please.

16
00:01:15,511 --> 00:01:28,800
[Q2答案句] That's 17, Buckleigh Street-B-U-C-K-L-E-I-G-H Street, Stamford, Lincolnshire,

17
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:35,017
though you don't really need the county. Oh, I know Stamford - it's a lovely town.

18
00:01:35,017 --> 00:01:36,801
(Q3) And what's the postcode?&nbsp;

19
00:01:36,801 --> 00:01:41,589
[Q3答案句] PE9 7QT

20
00:01:41,589 --> 00:01:46,776
(Q4) Right, thank you. So are you working here, or are you a student?

21
00:01:46,776 --> 00:01:53,605
I started studying at the university a couple of weeks ago, and I've got a part-time job for a few hours a week.

22
00:01:53,605 --> 00:01:57,358
What do you do? Well, I've done several different things.

23
00:01:57,358 --> 00:02:04,168
[Q4答案句+⭕️干扰项] I've just finished a short-term contract as a courier, and now I'm working as a waiter in one of the big hotels.

24
00:02:04,168 --> 00:02:07,317
Uhuh. That can't leave you much time for studying!

25
00:02:07,317 --> 00:02:10,415
Oh, it's not too bad. I manage to fit it all in.&nbsp;

26
00:02:10,415 --> 00:02:12,165
(Q5) What are you studying?

27
00:02:12,165 --> 00:02:17,738
[Q5答案句] My ambition is to go into parliament eventually, so my major subject is politics.

28
00:02:17,738 --> 00:02:23,298
That's partly why I think the Youth Council is important and want to be a part of it.

29
00:02:23,298 --> 00:02:30,255
And I suppose you've also taking a minor subject, aren't you? I know a lot of people study economics too.

30
00:02:30,255 --> 00:02:36,088
I chose history. To be honest, I'm not finding it as interesting as I expected!

31
00:02:36,088 --> 00:02:43,229
(Q6) OK, so with your studying and your part-time job, do you have time for any other interests or hobbies?

32
00:02:43,229 --> 00:02:50,039
[Q6答案句] Well, I spend quite a lot of time cycling both around town to get to university and to work,

33
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:53,353
and also long-distance, from here to London, for instance.

34
00:02:53,353 --> 00:02:56,768
(Q7) [🟢 anything else = and] That's pretty impressive! Anything else?

35
00:02:56,768 --> 00:03:04,767
[Q7答案句] For relaxation I'm also keen on the cinema - I used to go at least once a week，but I can't manage to go so often now.

36
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:09,391
(Q8) Right. Are you sure you'll have enough time for the Youth Council?

37
00:03:09,391 --> 00:03:14,627
Yes, I've worked out that I can afford to reduce my hours at work, and that will make the time.

38
00:03:14,627 --> 00:03:19,738
[🟢Q7定位 专有名词] So is there any particular aspect of the Youth Council's work that appeals to you, Roger?

39
00:03:19,738 --> 00:03:30,282
[Q8答案句] Well my sister is blind, so I'm particularly interested in working with disabled young people, to try and improve the quality of their lives.

40
00:03:30,282 --> 00:03:36,681
(Q9) That's great. Well, the best way to get involved is to be nominated by some people who you know.

41
00:03:36,681 --> 00:03:40,390
Right. Can you tell me how to set about organising that?

42
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:44,399
[🟢 定位 专有名词] You should talk to Jeffrey, our Elections Officer.

43
00:03:44,399 --> 00:03:49,047
I can arrange a meeting in the council office with him, if you like. Yes, please.

44
00:03:49,047 --> 00:03:52,901
He'll be here next Monday, if that suits you.

45
00:03:52,901 --> 00:03:58,029
That's the 14th, isn't it? Yes. I can manage late afternoon.

46
00:03:58,029 --> 00:04:03,301
Would you like to suggest a time? He generally leaves around 5.30.

47
00:04:03,301 --> 00:04:11,100
[Q9答案句+等确定] Well, would 4.30 be OK? My last class finishes at 4, so I'd have plenty of time to get to your office.

48
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:13,046
Right, that's fine.&nbsp;

49
00:04:13,046 --> 00:04:16,864
(Q10) Oh, and could I have a phone number we can contact you on?

50
00:04:16,864 --> 00:04:25,638
[Q10答案句] Yes, my mobile number's 07788 136711.

51
00:04:25,638 --> 00:04:30,039
Thank you. Well, well look forward to seeing you next week.

52
00:04:30,039 --> 00:04:32,539
Thanks very much. Goodbye. Bye.

